+# Incidents brief, August–September 2026
+
+## 11 August: ingestion stall, full disk
+
+- **Impact:** Data intake stopped for 2.5 hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+- **Cause:** A malformed batch jammed ingestion; endless retries filled the database disk.
+- **Fix:** Set the bad batch aside, then freed disk space.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Disk alert at 80%: no owner; open (85% again in September, spotted by chance).
+  - Stop bad batches jamming ingestion: Jonas; open.
+  - Paging escalation, 15 minutes per step: Elif, Sunil; done (30 September meeting).
+  - Purge the old 30-minute figure from handbook: Mara; open.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+- **Impact:** Public API down 47 minutes on a Monday morning; nearly all clients failed to connect.
+- **Cause:** The certificate expired; renewal had failed silently since early September (outdated credential).
+- **Fix:** Renewed the certificate, restarted the API.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Fix renewal, alert on failure: no owner; done.
+  - Reminder 14 days before expiry: no owner; open.
+  - Alert on days remaining: no owner; open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist: no owner; open.
+  - Record steps during incidents: incident handler; standing practice.
+
+Open = no source records it as done.
